> A hand-checkable calculation

For one action with reward2 and continuation probability.5, discount.8 gives V=2+.4V=10/3. The continuation deficit represents terminal outcomes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dynamic_programming_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
